.Dd July 27, 2026
.Dt SECUREDKIM-SIGN 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm securedkim-sign
.Nd command-line DKIM signing tool
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Fl d Ar domain
.Fl s Ar selector
.Fl k Ar keyfile
.Op Fl a Ar algorithm
.Op Fl c Ar canon
.Op Fl -headers Ar list
.Op Fl -oversign Ar list
.Op Fl l
.Op Fl -no-timestamp
.Op Fl -no-normalize
.Ar message-file
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
signs an RFC 5322 message file with the same signing code path
.Xr securedkim 8
uses, and writes the signed message \(em a new DKIM-Signature header
prepended to the original file, unchanged \(em to standard output.
.Pp
The original file is emitted rather than a reconstruction of it, because the
point of
.Nm
is to produce a signature another implementation can verify, and a verifier
reading the output must see exactly the message that was signed.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Fl d Ar domain
Signing domain
.Pq Cm d= .
Required.
.It Fl s Ar selector
Selector
.Pq Cm s= .
Required.
.It Fl k Ar keyfile
Private key file.
Required.
PEM format for
.Cm rsa-sha256 ;
for
.Cm ed25519-sha256 ,
a file holding the base64 encoding of the 32-byte seed, which is what
.Xr securedkim-genkey 8
emits.
An RSA key is held to the RFC 8301 1024-bit floor and refused if its
permissions are readable beyond its owner, exactly as
.Cm SignKeyFile
is in
.Xr securedkim 8 .
.It Fl a Ar algorithm
Signing algorithm:
.Dq rsa-sha256
(default) or
.Dq ed25519-sha256 .
.It Fl c Ar canon
Canonicalization, as
.Ar header Ns / Ns Ar body :
.Dq relaxed/relaxed
(default),
.Dq simple/simple ,
.Dq relaxed/simple ,
or
.Dq simple/relaxed .
.It Fl -headers Ar list
Colon-separated
.Cm h=
list.
Default:
.Dq from:to:subject:date:message-id .
.It Fl -oversign Ar list
Colon-separated names to list once more than the message contains them, so
that a later addition of one of those headers breaks the signature.
Default:
.Dq from .
An empty string disables oversigning.
.It Fl l
Include
.Cm l=
covering the whole canonicalized body.
.It Fl -no-timestamp
Omit
.Cm t= ,
so output is byte-stable across runs.
.It Fl -no-normalize
Do not rewrite a bare CR or LF in the file to CRLF while reading it.
On by default for the same reason
.Xr securedkim-check 8 Ap s
flag of the same name is: an
.Pa .eml
file edited on a Unix host is usually LF-only, and DKIM is defined over CRLF.
.It Fl h , Fl -help
Display usage information.
Note that
.Fl h
is help here, not the
.Cm h=
list \(em
.Nm opendkim
and
.Nm dkimpy
spell the
.Cm h=
list
.Fl h ,
so this tool uses the long
.Fl -headers
instead of letting
.Fl h
quietly mean something else.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Bl -tag -width indent -compact
.It 0
The message was signed and written to standard output.
.It 2
The tool could not run: bad arguments, an unreadable or unparsable message
file, a key that could not be loaded, or a canonicalization or signing
failure.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
Sign a message with an RSA key, default headers:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
securedkim-sign -d example.com -s 2026 -k /usr/local/etc/securedkim/example.key \e
    message.eml > signed.eml
.Ed
.Pp
Sign with Ed25519 and a fixed timestamp, for byte-reproducible output:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
securedkim-sign -a ed25519-sha256 -d example.com -s ed2026 -k ed-key.seed \e
    --no-timestamp message.eml
.Ed
.Pp
Sign with
.Cm l=
and oversigning disabled:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
securedkim-sign -d example.com -s 2026 -k example.key -l --oversign "" message.eml
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr securedkim 8 ,
.Xr securedkim-check 8 ,
.Xr securedkim-genkey 8 ,
.Xr securedkim-testkey 8
.Sh STANDARDS
.Rs
.%T DomainKeys Identified Mail (DKIM) Signatures
.%R RFC 6376
.Re
.Rs
.%T Use of RSA-SHA-256 and Ed25519-SHA-256 in DKIM
.%R RFC 8463
.Re
.Sh AUTHORS
.An Daniel Morante
